# More Than A Hack 2027 - Match Possession Classification Pipeline

A high-performing, end-to-end machine learning pipeline designed to classify frame-by-frame match possession (`H`, `A`, `D`, `X`) for the **More Than A Hack 2027** hackathon (Metrica Sports & FC Barcelona).

---

## Overview
This repository implements an advanced automated tracking analysis pipeline that processes EPTS optical coordinates (`.txt`) and tactical smart-tagging event logs (`.xml`) to predict continuous possession spells for FC Barcelona (`H`) and Athletic Club (`A`), alongside dead-ball (`D`) and unknown transition (`X`) states. 

The architecture bridges raw spatial coordinates with kinematic velocity vectors, multi-frame rolling memory, confidence-based abstention, and mathematical latency alignment to optimize both **Macro F1** and **Spell F1 (`spellF1`)** metrics.

---

## Key Technical Features
1. **Kinematic Feature Engineering:** Computes instantaneous player and ball velocity vectors ($\Delta x, \Delta y$), maximum closing speeds towards the ball, and dynamic team centroids.
2. **Advanced Spatial Proximity:** Evaluates team-specific minimum distances, spatial control differentials (`dist_diff`), active duels, and ball playability states.
3. **Short-Term Memory:** Implements 10-frame ($0.4\text{s}$) and 25-frame ($1.0\text{s}$) rolling averages to capture sustained pressure and spatial control.
4. **Class-Balanced XGBoost:** Utilizes sample-weight balancing to prevent majority dead-ball class dominance.
5. **Post-Processing & Latency Correction:** Employs confidence thresholds, forward-fill smoothing, absolute dead-ball overrides, and a 12-frame mathematical temporal shift to neutralize optical transition latency and maximize spell Intersection over Union (IoU).

---

